--- body ---
## Context

Failing tests (all same root cause):
- `tests/test_harness.py::test_web_search_model_gets_plugin`
- `tests/test_harness.py::test_both_capabilities`
- `tests/test_query_frontier.py::test_web_search_model_gets_plugin`
- `tests/test_query_frontier.py::test_both_reasoning_and_web_search`

`src/aedist/harness.py:314` defines `build_api_kwargs(..., enable_web_search: bool = False)`. When a model has `web_search: true`, the function only injects `kwargs["tools"]` if `enable_web_search=True`. Tests construct a `model` dict with `web_search: True` but call `build_api_kwargs` without the flag → no `tools` key → KeyError.

**Fix: update the 4 tests to pass `enable_web_search=True`.**

Call-site audit (reimagine phase): only `worker.py` passes the flag
(forwarding `job.web_search`). All other production callers — `query.py`,
`query_web.py`, `query_rag.py`, `query_multiturn.py`, `query_decomposed.py`,
`query_frontier.py` — omit it, relying on the `False` default. Flipping
the default would silently enable web search in all those callers
(~$0.02/call costs + non-determinism). The tests simply forgot to pass the
flag they are testing.

## Actions

1. `rg 'build_api_kwargs\(' src/ scripts/ experiments/` — audit call-sites.
2. Decide default based on majority behavior. Document decision in one-line comment at the signature.
3. Apply the fix; run the 4 failing tests + the rest of the harness suite.

## Test

Existing 4 tests are the regression test. No new tests needed.

## Exit criteria

- All 4 tests pass.
- No regressions in `tests/test_harness.py` or `tests/test_query*.py`.
- Full suite (minus other red clusters tracked by 0107-0110) green.
